    "body": "SALVADOR_REAL_PROJECT_VISUAL_EVALUATION_R02\n\nCLASS = TRAINING DIAGNOSIS / REAL PROJECT / SIMPLIFICATION BOUNDARY\nPROMOTION = NO\nCERTIFICATION = NO\nHOLDOUT = NO\nGENERALIZATION_CLAIM = NO\nPROFILE_CHANGE = NO\nMODEL_CHANGE = NO\nPROMPT_CHANGE = NO\nWORKFLOW_CHANGE = NO\n\nSOURCE_REFERENCE_SHA256 = 0f4483658d634f30d13707c1675186b22c6c127732a17f9b3a07d48693f0c58f\nSOURCE_DIMENSIONS = 1024x1536\nCANDIDATE_A_CLEAN_SHA256 = 93ae9784f6b6bc547701890c732043b578b62068f8af38116e76638b219857ac\nCANDIDATE_A_DIMENSIONS = 1024x1536\nCANDIDATE_B_AGGRESSIVE_SHA256 = adb0dbeffe04725835e2f1e9b620e6e5811e0f1e6a3213d35552c692ec0eb486\nCANDIDATE_B_DIMENSIONS = 1024x1536\n\nSOURCE_VISIBLE_LOCKS:\n- stern angular face read\n- dark dreadlock mass tied/gathered behind head\n- dark open shirt over light undershirt\n- wide gray trouser mass\n- dark belt + loafers\n- neck/chest/forearm tattoo zones with branching directional topology\n- hands-in-pockets stance inherited from the available source reference\n\nCANDIDATE_A_CLEAN:\nFACE_IDENTITY = PASS\nHAIR_MASS = PASS\nBODY_BUILD = PASS\nGARMENT_ARCHITECTURE = PASS\nSILHOUETTE = PASS\nTATTOO_ZONE_PLACEMENT = PASS\nTATTOO_DIRECTIONAL_LANGUAGE = PASS\nDETAIL_REDUCTION = PASS\nFOLD_REDUCTION = PASS\nPOSE_PRESERVATION = PASS\nCANDIDATE_A_RESULT = PASS\n\nCANDIDATE_B_AGGRESSIVE:\nSILHOUETTE = PASS\nHAIR_MASS = PASS\nGARMENT_MAJOR_ZONES = PASS\nBODY_BUILD = PASS\nTATTOO_ZONE_PLACEMENT = PASS\nTATTOO_SPECIFIC_TOPOLOGY = FAIL\nFACIAL_SPECIFICITY = PARTIAL\nDETAIL_REDUCTION = OVER_BUDGET\nCANDIDATE_B_RESULT = CHANGES_REQUIRED\n\nROOT_CAUSE = Candidate B reduces information density past the character-specificity floor. Large tattoo zones survive, but distinctive branching flow/topology collapses toward generic jagged patches; facial construction is also normalized more strongly than Candidate A. This is over-simplification, not permission to redesign.\n\nIMPORTANT_NON_FAILURE = Hands remain in pockets because that pose exists in the available source reference. Do not import unrelated technical-front requirements unless the active task explicitly requires visible hands. SOURCE-SCOPED REQUIREMENTS OVERRIDE GENERIC TEMPLATE HABITS.\n\nNEW_TRAINING_LAWS:\n1. LOWER INFORMATION DENSITY != LOWER CHARACTER SPECIFICITY.\n2. DETAIL REDUCTION HAS A FLOOR: remove microdetail, not identity-bearing topology.\n3. ZONE PRESERVATION ALONE IS INSUFFICIENT when directional/topological structure is identity-bearing.\n4. CLEANER IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY BETTER; the least-detailed candidate can be worse if specificity collapses.\n5. TASK-SCOPED SOURCE REQUIREMENTS outrank unrelated generic front-view habits.\n6. POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE CANDIDATES SHOULD BE COMPARED AGAINST THE SAME SOURCE to learn the simplification boundary.\n\nREAL_PROJECT_SAMPLES_COMPLETED = 2\nR01_ARTWORK_MODELS_REVIEWED = 8\nR02_BOUNDARY_CANDIDATES_REVIEWED = 2\nCRITICAL = 0\nUNSUPPORTED_GUESS = 0\n\nREAL_VISUAL_TRAINING_R01 = PASS\nPASS_MEANING = two independent real-project training samples produced actionable preservation laws and correctly separated artwork quality, evidence quality, and over-simplification failure.\nSHADOW_STATE_PROMOTION = NO\nEXPECTED_SKILL_EFFECT = PARTIAL_ONLY\n\nDURABLE_CONTINUATION_FROM = PR #171 HEAD 75760f616130fab9f16193de3666e0a5982d57fa\nPREVIOUS_REAL_SAMPLE_COMMENT = 5462221109",
